{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses","id":936778,"title":"Scenario: What if the Wyrm looses?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-24T16:20:12-07:00","id":936778,"title":"Scenario: What if the Wyrm looses?","content":"I've ended a big time of judgement crossover, but instead of destroying the world had the outcome end with the good guy winning. In one of the final battle scenarios, the garou and fera clans reunite and systematically begin destroying the maeljin incarna, slayed number two at the room of mystery, sealed the entrance to the labyrinth in the temple obscura, opened the wyld founts, and generally blew malfeas to smithereens. In the end malfeas was consumed by flux and the digital web, and along with it the wyrm was devoured by the wyld and weaver.<br /> <br /> Now what?<br /> <br /> How do I portray the new world without the wyrm? What happens to the garou? Are the weaver and wyld trapped in an eternal chess match now that there's no third party? How should I run future games now that our world of grey morality has lost an ugly black splotch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T18:59:32-07:00","id":936842,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm cannot be devoured because the Weaver and the Wyld are incapable of destruction. However, if it did happen, there would no longer be death and destruction. <br /> <br /> The Wyrm is death and destruction, two necessary forces. Without the Wyrm, atoms cannot fuse to create sunlight, atoms cannot fision to create geothermal heat, plants cannot die to feed animals, animals cannot die to feed humans, and humans cannot die to make room for new generations. Without the Wyrm, everything descends into a dark and frozen Hell of eternal starvation and overpopulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T22:18:40-07:00","id":936933,"title":"","content":"So I do agree that the Wyrm should not be able to be devoured.<br /> <br /> And I agree Death might very well cease to exist if you did go that route. I don't agree with &quot;everything descends into a dark and frozen Hell of eternal starvation and overpopulation.&quot;<br /> <br /> The world could become a battleground between flux and stasis. Nothing can die, but it can be mutated or changed. Starvation may or may not even matter. With the stasis part, I think universal sterility might very well be a solution to the relatively minor problem of overpopulation. You could have an effect where whenever anything should die, it instead reforms into a new...something. Doesn't really matter what. Maybe light, maybe a new creature. The being might just come back a few minutes later having reformed.<br /> <br /> You could also just have the Dragon of Pangea ascend and take up the role of the Wyrm of Balance. That would have far less reality warping effects and allow you to continue the game with more mild changes. Have Pangea push through into the material world in pockets. I'm not sure how you've had the Apocalypse affect your material world so far, so it's a bit tough to figure out what can/should happen because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T22:29:58-07:00","id":936934,"title":"","content":"I would imagine with out a common enemy the garou nation would tear itself apart","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T06:16:31-07:00","id":937030,"title":"","content":"The corruption of the Wyrm is just part of a greater cycle. The Weaver becomes more and more powerful as a sapient species becomes dominant and, over the course of a couple of million years, the Weaver traps the Wyrm. After the Weaver traps the Wyrm, the sapient species experiences rapid technological advancement until that species causes a mass extinction event or until the Wyrm causes a mass extinction event. With the Weaver weakened, the Wyrm is released and, through its very nature, achieves balance through destroying its own corruption. <br /> <br /> While no member of the Triat can be destroyed (at least not without the destroyer immediately replacing that member of the Triat), they can be weakened. The Garou will only stop the corruption of the Wyrm by weakening the Weaver enough to allow the Wyrm to escape its trap. The easy way of doing that is the reduce the population of the human species by 95%, perhaps through a nuclear exchange, where the majority of the people would die of famine and plague after the nuclear exchange destroys the infrastructure required to maintain the population of human and creates a nuclear winter that reduces global food production by 90% for a decade. The hard way of doing that is the reduce human consumption by technological progress and social change.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the hard way has not worked because of the nature of human kind, so the Garou must do the easy way. If they do not, the Wyrm will do it for them and they will likely go extinction with everything else. If the Garou united and worked with the Fera, they could save their kinfolk (human and animal) against the effects of the easy way. If they do not, they will all die when the Wyrm breaks free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T06:19:19-07:00","id":937034,"title":"","content":"The second Book of the Wyrm mentioned that the Wyrm wants to die so a newer and saner form can emerge. Now the question would be if all the Wyrm's most twisted minions died with him, change to a saner form (like the BSD turning back into White Howlers) or would some of them remain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T10:49:52-07:00","id":937171,"title":"","content":"Yes, balance through destruction. I would suggest that any banes would eventually be purified without the support of the Wyrm, but I think that it would take a few centuries. The BSD would gradually lose access to their Gifts and their Rites, as the corrupted spirits that they depend on start to ignore them when they are purified, until they are incapable of using any of the magic of the Garou. Eventually, the BSD population would drop to the point where they could not kill off White Howlers as they are born and the White Howlers would start to reemerge as a clan. Whether Lion would choose to sponsor them or if Bat would remain their Totem would depend on factors beyond this conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T10:55:57-07:00","id":937173,"title":"","content":"Should the Wyrm die, it is unclear whether Gaia, The Wyld, The Weaver, or all three of them acting in concert, could recreate the Untainted Dissolver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:16:42-07:00","id":937209,"title":"","content":"They do not have to, the Wyrm will destroy the tainted aspects of itself when it is free of the bonds placed on it by the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T13:28:19-07:00","id":937252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=937209#post937209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do not have to, the Wyrm will destroy the tainted aspects of itself when it is free of the bonds placed on it by the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that in the scenario presented by the OP the Wyrm doesn't get freed. It was apparently consumed by the Weaver and Wyld.<br /> <br /> It's an odd scenario I think. But presented with that, I would assume one of the other Wyrm-type entities that aren't corrupted might be elevated to become the Wyrm of Balance. I would vote for either the Dragon of Pangea or whatever the most powerful Wani spirit is. Maybe a third entity could be combined with those 2 to create a new triatic Wyrm entity.<br /> Either way, the Wyrm of Balance should be restored/reinstated and though weaker, the world should go on closer to the same than if you have one of the 3 fundamental entity-forces of the universe just disappear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T13:59:06-07:00","id":937271,"title":"","content":"Yes, though the Wyrm of Balance would end up growing in power until it was balanced with other two (thus the name).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:01:06-07:00","id":937313,"title":"","content":"That should take a lot longer than the Chronicle runs. So for all intents and purposes, for the remainder of the game the Triat would be out of balance and the world would be different because of it.<br /> <br /> If you accept that premise, then there is the decision that need to be made on just how the world will differ from before the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:19:03-07:00","id":937324,"title":"","content":"When I wrote up the weaver and wyld devour the wyrm thing, I meant it to also represent how the weaver and wyld now take over the important aspects of the wyrm.<br /> <br /> The wyld is already an agent of both corruption and change(in that its changes are random and equally likely to be either helpful or detrimental without some form of control), so now it also becomes the owner of death and entropy(with &quot;Death&quot; being the proccess that changes a living being into another form(IE dirt) and &quot;entropy&quot; as the a combination of mage entropy and thermodynamic entropy(all systems no matter how orderly always descend into greater chaos))<br /> <br /> The Weaver was always an agent of control and logic over free will, and now rules physical decay(That all systems of energy will eventually balance out, losing their energy and returning to nothing).<br /> <br /> If nothing else this should happen at least temporarily until a new Wyrm rises to take its mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:25:12-07:00","id":937330,"title":"","content":"I don't think they (The Wyld and Weaver) <i>can</i> take over those functions. That sort of thing is possibly what started this whole out of balance thing in the first place. The Weaver stepping outside of it's function and destroying something is supposedly when Queen Ananasa realized &quot;he&quot; had gone insane. I think having both aspects step outside of their function would actually be more detrimental to the universe as a whole than the Wyrm going crazy ever was. And it would happen much much faster this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T18:36:12-07:00","id":937393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=937330#post937330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they (The Wyld and Weaver) <i>can</i> take over those functions. That sort of thing is possibly what started this whole out of balance thing in the first place. The Weaver stepping outside of it's function and destroying something is supposedly when Queen Ananasa realized &quot;he&quot; had gone insane. I think having both aspects step outside of their function would actually be more detrimental to the universe as a whole than the Wyrm going crazy ever was. And it would happen much much faster this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, maybe? The wyrm never seemed, well, necessary in the first place to me both ic and ooc. IC the wyrm represents a force that could easily be covered by the other two, while OOC it represents an unnecessary evil enemy when the story could work just as well with the other two more complex and morally grey enemies. Even pentex could work as the megacorp of greedy ceo's with some knowledge of the supernatural with or without a &quot;Wyrm&quot; to serve. They could be fucking up the world not for their demon overlords, but instead secretly running their illegal, immoral, and/or mystical/demonic operations for the actual profit(I'm very sure the local vampires would pay top dollar for a device that detects werewolves and their caerns for instance)<br /> <br /> Though I guess that's just my opinion though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T19:22:29-07:00","id":937408,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm is essential because destruction supplies chaos with essence when order is destroyed. Without the Wyrm, the Wyld runs out of essence. Without the Wyrm, the Weaver achieves perfect stasis and everything comes to a halt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T19:49:50-07:00","id":937416,"title":"","content":"Your campaign is over. It is finished. Nothing more to do. You just destroyed Satan and blew up Hell. The World to Come has arrived, and your chronicle has fulfilled the eschatological implications inherent in the setting. Congratulate your players on a job well done. At most, you just need to describe an epilogue (confirming for them this new world without evil) and begin discussion with your players on what to do next. And if you still want to play Werewolf, what kind of game they want to do in a world where your Time of Judgment hasn't happened.<br /> <br /> The only way you could continue is for the Garou Nation to learn that in fact, they were completely wrong about the nature of the spirit world and the Triat. For the past 10,000 years they have believed and followed a lie, and after great sacrifice nothing has essentially changed. They've done the impossible, and yet they've still failed. Most likely mass Harano would follow. The Garou and Changing Breeds die off, and only a few survivors will exist in a few decades trying to figure out all the questions you just posed in the original post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T19:52:45-07:00","id":937418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=937408#post937408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrm is essential because destruction supplies chaos with essence when order is destroyed. Without the Wyrm, the Wyld runs out of essence. Without the Wyrm, the Weaver achieves perfect stasis and everything comes to a halt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you know, chaos could do that on its own like in most other order vs chaos cosmologies in literature. The entropy thing just seems kinda tacked on to me, but again that is just my opinion. I am aware though that the wyld and weaver aren't so much &quot;chaos and order&quot; as &quot;change and stasis&quot;. Though this seems watered down to me, again, it is just my opinion.<br /> <br /> To take us back on the main topic, how would death work in a world where the wyrm is temporarily(or permanently) &quot;indisposed&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=937408#post937408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">our campaign is over. It is finished. Nothing more to do. You just destroyed Satan and blew up Hell. The World to Come has arrived, and your chronicle has fulfilled the eschatological implications inherent in the setting. Congratulate your players on a job well done. At most, you just need to describe an epilogue (confirming for them this new world without evil) and begin discussion with your players on what to do next. And if you still want to play Werewolf, what kind of game they want to do in a world where your Time of Judgment hasn't happened.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The only way you could continue is for the Garou Nation to learn that in fact, they were completely wrong about the nature of the spirit world and the Triat. For the past 10,000 years they have believed and followed a lie, and after great sacrifice nothing has essentially changed. They've done the impossible, and yet they've still failed. Most likely mass Harano would follow. The Garou and Changing Breeds die off, and only a few survivors will exist in a few decades trying to figure out all the questions you just posed in the original post.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">That is kinda not what I'm going for, not to mention the world is far from&quot;Without evil&quot; as the weaver is still intent on calcifying the world and the wyld is free to play with the chaos of the aftermath.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 07-25-2016, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T20:27:04-07:00","id":937431,"title":"","content":"A world without the Wyrm is a world without death, and there is nothing more horrible than the idea of a world without death. Cancer cells will continue to grow within the body, unchecked by the cells around them. Bacteria, parasites, and viruses will turn human beings into walking plague pits. Without death, suffering does not end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T20:36:17-07:00","id":937437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=937418#post937418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To take us back on the main topic, how would death work in a world where the wyrm is temporarily(or permanently) &quot;indisposed&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It might stop. Torchwood did a whole season dealing with the Death no longer happening. You could take inspiration from there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T21:23:41-07:00","id":938582,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm's purpose is the cleansing and rectification of Creation, furthering its descent into Entropy. He achieves this by eliminating that which the Wyld creates and the Weaver structures. If the Wyrm isn't there, the Wyld will keep creating and there's none to throw the trash out (which he Wyrm used to do) while the Weaver keeps structuring endlessly, your world will basically come to an end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","user":"Darko","date":". 07-28-2016, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:37:08-07:00","id":939188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=938582#post938582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrm's purpose is the cleansing and rectification of Creation, furthering its descent into Entropy. He achieves this by eliminating that which the Wyld creates and the Weaver structures. If the Wyrm isn't there, the Wyld will keep creating and there's none to throw the trash out (which he Wyrm used to do) while the Weaver keeps structuring endlessly, your world will basically come to an end.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least not immediately. It would take a while to overrun the earth, probably long enough for the garou to find a replacement &quot;Balance Wyrm&quot; that isn't corrupt. Or they fail and earth becomes an eternal living hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T18:39:37-07:00","id":939257,"title":"","content":"Yep, that is my thoughts on the matter... It is better to free the Wyrm from the Weaver, to allow its own annihilation, so that it can purge the corruption from its spirit, though it is necessary for anyone sensible to destroy the agents of the Wyrm of Corruption until it becomes again the Wyrm of Balance..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T15:35:57-07:00","id":939831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=939257#post939257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, that is my thoughts on the matter... It is better to free the Wyrm from the Weaver, to allow its own annihilation, so that it can purge the corruption from its spirit, though it is necessary for anyone sensible to destroy the agents of the Wyrm of Corruption until it becomes again the Wyrm of Balance..</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything of the wyrm of balance is left, it might just be an even worse corrupting wyrm trapped in the weavers web.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T06:03:07-07:00","id":940593,"title":"","content":"It's funny... back in 1st and 2nd edition, this probably wouldn't be considered a remote possibility. And while I like the way that Revised and W20 undid some rather overblown aspects (e.g. Nazi Fenrir), it also sort of whitewashed what I'd considered an important theme of the game- The Garou stood no chance and it was almost entirely their fault. The amount of politics, backbiting, posturing, and petty quarreling and feuds (all fueled by supernatural Rage no human could comprehend) made it impossible for them to ever unify in name of the greater good, let alone mend bridges with the Fera they betrayed and murdered. Reading the fluff nowadays, and you'd think BoneGnawers and Metis walked on water. But that's neither here nor there, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, &quot;killing&quot; the Wyrm I think has two possible outcomes:<br /> 1) As a manifestation of a kind of primordial element of existence, I'd wager that regardless of how the &quot;old Wyrm&quot; goes, a new one would manifest to fill the void. Kind of like how the books gently hint with the delicacy of a sledgehammer that various human religions/technologies/ideas have spawned Incarna/Celestine-level spirits. If someone, somehow, destroyed the spiritual manifestation of Santa Claus, there might be some sort of echo in the physical world... but Christmas wouldn't disappear. More likely, the continued belief would re-embody a new spiritual representation. (This is where I would put my money)<br /> <br /> 2) The Wyrm dies, and therefore the force it represents stops working. The world is now the Weaver's to calcify to its heart's content. Sure, the Wyld still makes stuff here and there, but the Weaver has been gaining immense power for a while now. The next fight would be battling to prevent all existence from becoming a theater of frozen scenery and statues. How they might fight that battle would be interesting, because who even knows how concepts like death would now operate.<br /> <br /> Overall, though, I think Aya Tari has it right. The Weaver is actually responsible for starting the series of events that led to all this... so whether you get a new Wyrm or not, the Weaver has to be dealt with somehow to prevent either the cycle from repeating itself, or the universe from becoming locked in place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T07:46:27-07:00","id":940619,"title":"","content":"The question is how do you deal with the Weaver without causing more problems? One possibility that is mentioned in passing in the Book of the Weaver (Revised) is the rescue of the Science Incarna from being completely absorbed into the Machine Incarna. I am not quite sure how to do that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:08:23-07:00","id":940622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=940619#post940619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is how do you deal with the Weaver without causing more problems?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think this is a similar problem to fighting the Wyrm. How do you destroy something that feeds on destruction? The Weaver is a fundamental force... It's the reason things have shape. Violence might be useful in weakening the Weaver and its minions to a limited extent (which is handy, since that's at the top of the Garous' bag of tricks)... But healing the Weaver's madness and obsession is honestly the only option that doesn't involve direct intervention from celestial powers (and honestly still might need a nudge or two of their assistance) or restarting the whole dang universe.<br /> <br /> Maybe there'sa way to just finish off the rest of the triat... If that happened either everything would be balanced by all three's absence (or the universe might end, who knows?). Or it might provide the balance and vacuum needed to reform all three again from the start. Make the whole triat reroll fresh characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:15:01-07:00","id":940675,"title":"","content":"Which would probably reset the Universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:25:07-07:00","id":940715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=940675#post940675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would probably reset the Universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you run spirits in a story, that they are the things they embody and their destruction also destroys that thing, or that they represent the thing they embody and are born and reborn so long as the thing exists. I tend to lean towards the latter as nothing outside the middle umbra actually gives a damn about the triat or gaia, so they don't really seem That important to the universe as a whole.(also because I run that the middle, high, and low umbra are earth's and only earth's umbra, and that other, more alien worlds would have their own umbras. Making the triat and gaia earth's personal supernals, not the entire universe's)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:31:45-07:00","id":940748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=940715#post940715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on how you run spirits in a story, that they are the things they embody and their destruction also destroys that thing, or that they represent the thing they embody and are born and reborn so long as the thing exists. I tend to lean towards the latter as nothing outside the middle umbra actually gives a damn about the triat or gaia, so they don't really seem That important to the universe as a whole.(also because I run that the middle, high, and low umbra are earth's and only earth's umbra, and that other, more alien worlds would have their own umbras. Making the triat and gaia earth's personal supernals, not the entire universe's)</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat understandable. I would say though for the purposes of most games, that the destruction of Earth and the destruction of the Universe could be pretty much the same to many involved.<br /> A lot of this hinges on the interpretation of the cosmology. I think for a Werewolf game I certainly disagree with the view you have, though it works fine for a Mage or Vampire game. In Werewolf, the Weaver Wyld and Wyrm do make up the universe. They are the universal forces. They aren't located <i>in</i> Gaia's Umbra.<br /> Your view changes quite a bit about how the Umbra works, the Aetherial Realm in particular. At least from an OOC point of view. In world, I suppose the inhabitants might not know the difference and so their view is correct for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:39:11-07:00","id":940754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/936778-scenario-what-if-the-wyrm-looses?p=940748#post940748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhat understandable. I would say though for the purposes of most games, that the destruction of Earth and the destruction of the Universe could be pretty much the same to many involved.<br /> A lot of this hinges on the interpretation of the cosmology. I think for a Werewolf game I certainly disagree with the view you have, though it works fine for a Mage or Vampire game. In Werewolf, the Weaver Wyld and Wyrm do make up the universe. They are the universal forces. They aren't located <i>in</i> Gaia's Umbra.<br /> Your view changes quite a bit about how the Umbra works, the Aetherial Realm in particular. At least from an OOC point of view. In world, I suppose the inhabitants might not know the difference and so their view is correct for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, I mostly like to run crossovers and focus on roleplay(even with all the problems such games entail), so I really only acknowledge the OOC for game mechanics and suggested themes. I find OWOD tend to work best if there is no &quot;One True Answer&quot; for everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:45:08-07:00","id":940761,"title":"","content":"I would actually say that it would involve the entire solar system, as there does seem to be a greater horizon that separates the spiritual solar system from the rest of the spiritual Universe. A dissolution of one or more of the triat would cause imbalances in the function of the Sun that would be disastrous. Without the Wyrm, fusion cannot turn matter into energy, so you would have Sol collapse into a white dwarf. Without the Wyld, the mixing with the Sun would stop, starving the Sun of fuel, which would cause a gravitational collapse and a white dwarf. Without the Weaver, gravity stops working, so the matter of the Sun (and atmosphere of every planet) would escape to the void (or turn the chocolate, as order would be gone).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:17:38-07:00","id":940794,"title":"","content":"I would say that knowing how you view the world/universe and how it differs from the &quot;normal&quot; Werewolf setting could have helped a lot for speculating the changes that would come from no longer having the Wyrm around. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}